WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Three recovery actions can have different consequences.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Observe, synchronize, rehearse, evaluate, and execute one action.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Existing simulator and physical recordings; estimated event alignment.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
A frozen normal-dynamics evaluator compares candidate responses.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Combine candidate-response costs with flight degradation, then select the minimum cost.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Recorded response comparisons support variable-dependent agreement.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:15.000
92.06% recovery-action agreement; this is distinct from measured recovery outcomes.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:42.000
Late-mission cases: Continue, Return, and Land under mild, moderate, and severe faults.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Ten mild-fault trials per strategy: 96.7% versus 36.1–37.7% progress; both recover in all ten trials.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Five seconds of collection plus 32.08 ms median overhead; physical actuation delay is not measured.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:29.000
Existing real-flight recordings illustrate the dynamics of recovery manoeuvres.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Rehearse before execute: retain recoverable missions and evaluate intervention consequences.
